invariant: INV-26
file: quic_packet.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: the 1-RTT open path never calls an aes_ entry by name. It stores
  the address of aes_encrypt_block_hp in a function pointer and calls
  through the pointer, so the call branch of
  inv-26-aes-public-keys-only binds its metavariable to mask_block and
  matches nothing. The value branch is what fires, on
  &aes_encrypt_block_hp. Without that branch the header protection key
  of a 1-RTT packet, which quic_hp_key_init derives from a TLS traffic
  secret, arrives at a lookup-table cipher and every check stays green.
  quic_packet.c is not one of the two callers the rule admits. Semgrep
  reads source text, so the edit needs no cast that compiles and no
  include; the rule matches the name either way.

--- old
void quic_hp_mask(const quic_hp_key *h, const uint8_t sample[QUIC_HP_SAMPLE_LEN],
                  uint8_t mask[QUIC_HP_MASK_LEN]) {
--- new
void quic_hp_mask(const quic_hp_key *h, const uint8_t sample[QUIC_HP_SAMPLE_LEN],
                  uint8_t mask[QUIC_HP_MASK_LEN]) {
    void (*mask_block)(const void *, const uint8_t *, uint8_t *) = &aes_encrypt_block_hp;
